-- title:
--   Two-torsion is nonempty
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group. Write $H=G[2]=\{x:2x=0\}$, $K=G[3]=\{x:3x=0\}$, $n=|G|$, $h=|H|$, and $t=|K|$. For a finite support $S$, let $Q_S(z)$ count ordered pairs in $S^2$ with sum $z$, let $F(S)$ be its fibre among three-element supports, and put $S+u=\{x+u:x\in S\}$. The two-torsion subgroup has positive cardinality: $$h>0.$$ In particular the trivial group is allowed.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/Strobo2TorsCardinality.lean, lines 328–330; source file SHA-256 43bb7bc977683362729a3aa2f7c214abefd9138f3283fb79ee93f0a1da784093; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.twoTorsion_card_pos

